{"datasheet_register_abbreviation": "PWR_CSR", "address_offset": "0x04", "reset_value": "0x00000000", "size": 32, "subfields": [{"name": "EWUP", "description": "Enable WKUP pin. This bit is set and cleared by software. 0: WKUP pin is used for general purpose I/O. An event on the WKUP pin does not wakeup the device from Standby mode. 1: WKUP pin is used for wakeup from Standby mode and forced in input pull down configuration (rising edge on WKUP pin wakes\u2011up the system from Standby mode). Note: This bit is reset by a system Reset.", "access": "read-write", "bit_number": {"start_bit": 8, "end_bit": 8}}, {"name": "PVDO", "description": "PVD output. This bit is set and cleared by hardware. It is valid only if PVD is enabled by the PVDE bit. 0: VDD/Vdda is higher than the PVD threshold selected with the PLS[2:0] bits. 1: VDD/Vdda is lower than the PVD threshold selected with the PLS[2:0] bits. Note: The PVD is stopped by Standby mode. For this reason, this bit is equal to 0 after Standby or reset until the PVDE bit is set.", "access": "read-only", "bit_number": {"start_bit": 2, "end_bit": 2}}, {"name": "SBF", "description": "Standby flag. This bit is set by hardware and cleared only by a POR/PDR (power on reset/power down reset) or by setting the CSBF bit in the Power control register (PWR_CR). 0: Device has not been in Standby mode. 1: Device has been in Standby mode.", "access": "read-only", "bit_number": {"start_bit": 1, "end_bit": 1}}, {"name": "WUF", "description": "Wakeup flag. This bit is set by hardware and cleared by hardware, by a system reset or by setting the CWUF bit in the Power control register (PWR_CR). 0: No wakeup event occurred. 1: A wakeup event was received from the WKUP pin or from the RTC alarm. Note: An additional wakeup event is detected if the WKUP pin is enabled (by setting the EWUP bit) when the WKUP pin level is already high.", "access": "read-only", "bit_number": {"start_bit": 0, "end_bit": 0}}], "access_constraints_v2": []}